 [{:id :s2a-wire/namespaced-key-alias-collapse
   :severity :P1 :confidence 1.0
   :location "src/oikos/infra/desktop_wire.cljc: lexical-ranges! # dispatch branch; decode-string owner read before inspect-tree!"
   :claim "Accepted namespaced maps can contain two lexical keys which resolve to the SAME owner key. Owner silently collapses the collision; the closed fresh tree and frozen law cannot detect the erased conflicting input. The candidate therefore does not meet the requested duplicate-key refusal profile."
   :reproduction {:runtimes [:bb :nbb]
                  :minimal "(wire/decode-string \"#:a{:x 1 :a/x 2}\") => #:a{:x 2}"
                  :equal-values "#:a{:x 1 :a/x 1} also accepted"
                  :reverse-order "#:a{:a/x 2 :x 1} => #:a{:x 1}"
                  :actual-event "Let base=(f/baseline), text=(clojure.string/replace (pr-str base) \":seq 1\" \":seq 999\"), ambiguous=(str (subs text 0 (dec (count text))) \" :event/seq 1}\"). (= base (wire/decode-event ambiguous)) returns true on both BB and NBB. Actual candidate default #:event output retained; no printer binding."
                  :owner-calls 1}
   :impact "Conflicting event sequence assertions disappear before qualification, so a wire event with :seq 999 and :event/seq 1 is accepted as the ordinary sequence-1 baseline with identical canonical identity. This is a concrete ambiguity/refusal failure, not a claim that a valid frozen event or approval was forged."
   :required "Add failing regressions for equal/unequal aliases in both orders and nested namespaces, including namespace-unqualification :_/x. Prevent ambiguous keys before the owner irreversibly collapses them. A carefully narrowed lexical map-key profile or reviewed additive owner duplicate-expansion refusal may solve it; do not copy an EDN/admission kernel or weaken frozen law. If owner source changes, new owner pin/digest/downstream review is required. Preserve actual default owner writer roundtrip."
   :existing-test-gap "only-explicit-bounded-namespaced-map-dispatch-is-admitted tests legal nesting and forbidden dispatch but not namespace-expanded key collisions."}
  {:id :s2a-wire/raw-partition-container-metadata-laundering
