   :claim "replay-history accepts a metadata-tainted raw in-memory partition vector, then mapv silently drops that metadata before frozen replay. This is not reader-generated location metadata and bypasses the strict raw-input boundary for the newly introduced container."
   :reproduction {:runtimes [:bb :nbb]
                  :expression "(let [v (with-meta [(pr-str (f/baseline))] {:secret \"SYNTHETIC-SECRET\"})] [(safe/plain-data? v) (:coverage (wire/replay-history (f/context) (f/revisions) v))])"
                  :actual [false :current]
                  :expected :constant-wire-invalid-refusal}
   :impact "A non-plain caller-owned runtime wrapper reaches decode/canonicalization and is laundered into plain partitions; the frozen law itself remains correct. This violates the stated preservation of raw caller metadata rejection, even though no metadata is serialized into the resulting event."
   :required "Before mapping or invoking owner functions require the captured-ledger container itself to satisfy the unchanged frozen plain-data representation guard (and existing vector/string/count limits). Add metadata variants including {}, location-only keys, secret and host/function metadata; assert constant refusal before owner parse/canonicalization. Do not strip container metadata."
   :existing-test-gap "Raw event metadata coverage is strong, but no metadata-bearing captured-ledgers vector is tested."}]
